IMPORT prelude
IMPORT `fp-claims`

-- Family Provision Act 1972 (WA) -- the questions people ask, with the seat and the situation as parameters (the Q&A
-- layer).
--
-- PURPOSE. One module whose exported questions serve every seat from one deployment. Every question takes `my role`
-- first ("Which of these describes you"); a question about another role answers `does not arise for you` without
-- reading any other input. The rules are the baseline's (fp-claims.l4): this layer builds the baseline's record (`My
-- position`) from plain answers and calls its functions. The administrator's protections the baseline does not encode
-- (s 20(1)-(3)) are added here as a helper.
--
-- ROLES. The family member who may claim (the baseline's seat); a beneficiary of the estate, whose share bears any
-- provision ordered (s 14(2)); and the executor or administrator, whom s 20 protects and s 7(2) and s 20(5) time. The
-- Supreme Court is never a seat. The Public Trustee may be the administrator (s 4(1)); the questions are worded for the
-- executor or administrator as a person and read the same for it.
--
-- SITUATIONS (design D8 of the Graffiti Vandalism Act layer). Within a role, a question that arises only in a
-- situation takes that situation's fact straight after `my role`, and when it does not hold answers `does not arise
-- for you` without reading anything else. The situations, each a BOOLEAN that gives `does not arise for you` when
-- FALSE: a grant of probate or administration in WA (s 7(2): the last day to apply without leave, for every role, and
-- whether the claimant's application is in time); a notice of an intended application given to the administrator
-- (s 20(5), claimant and administrator); for the claimant, an application made (s 7A), property not disclosed coming to
-- light (s 6(5)), provision ordered for me (s 14(2)), a dealing with my provision (s 19) and my written consent to a
-- distribution (s 20(4)); for the beneficiary, provision ordered for a claimant (s 14(2)); for the administrator, a
-- distribution made or proposed (s 20(1), (3), (4)). Who may claim, whether the will can shut a claim out, and whether
-- the Court can order provision arise for every claimant and take none.
--
-- BASELINE. Not for public use as advice. See NOTES.md, "Q&A layer (seat and situations as parameters)".

§ `Family Provision Act 1972 (WA) -- the questions people ask`

§§ `Who is asking, and the shape of the answers`

DECLARE Role IS ONE OF
    `I am a family member who may have been left out of the estate, or left too little`
    `I take a share of the estate under the will or on intestacy`
    `I am the executor or administrator of the estate`

DECLARE `Yes or no` IS ONE OF
    yes
    no
    `does not arise for you`

DECLARE `Amount` IS ONE OF
    `does not arise for you`
    amount HAS dollars IS A NUMBER

DECLARE `Date answer` IS ONE OF
    `does not arise for you`
    `by` HAS `the last day` IS A DATE
    `on` HAS `the day` IS A DATE

DECLARE `Standing answer` IS ONE OF
    `does not arise for you`
    `my standing is` HAS `which standing` IS A Standing

DECLARE `Timing answer` IS ONE OF
    `does not arise for you`
    `my application is` HAS `which timing` IS A Timing

DECLARE `Protection answer` IS ONE OF
    `does not arise for you`
    `no: section 20 bars that action against you`
    `section 20 does not bar it: whether the action lies is for the general law`

DECLARE `Outcome answer` IS ONE OF
    `does not arise for you`
    `the Court's power` HAS `which outcome` IS AN Outcome

§§ `Building the baseline's inputs, and the administrator's protection`

GIVEN `it holds` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A `Yes or no`
`yes if` `it holds` MEANS
    IF `it holds` THEN yes ELSE no

GIVEN `relationship` IS A Relationship
      `born` IS A `When I was born`
      `maintained` IS A BOOLEAN
      `entitled` IS A BOOLEAN
      `parent died first` IS A BOOLEAN
      `alive at the marriage` IS A BOOLEAN
      `took property` IS A BOOLEAN
      `its value` IS A NUMBER
      `parentage admitted` IS A BOOLEAN
      `artificial conception` IS A BOOLEAN
      `parent admitted` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A `My position`
`the position built from` MEANS
    `My position` WITH
        `my relationship to the deceased` IS `relationship`
        `when I was born` IS `born`
        `the deceased was maintaining me wholly or partly immediately before the death` IS `maintained`
        `I was entitled to be maintained by the deceased at the death` IS `entitled`
        `my parent, a child of the deceased, died before the deceased` IS `parent died first`
        `I was alive when the deceased married or began a de facto relationship with my parent` IS `alive at the marriage`
        `the deceased took property from my parent's estate, not as a creditor` IS `took property`
        `the value of that property at my parent's death` IS `its value`
        `the parentage I rely on was admitted or established in the parent's lifetime` IS `parentage admitted`
        `the parentage I rely on arises under the Artificial Conception Act 1985` IS `artificial conception`
        `as the parent, my parentage was admitted by the deceased as an adult or established in the deceased's lifetime` IS `parent admitted`

-- s 20(1): "No action shall lie against the administrator by reason of his having distributed any part of the estate, if
-- the distribution was properly made without notice of any application or intended application under this Act". (3): the
-- same for a person "whose relationship to the deceased is not determined through a legal marriage or adoption", without
-- the word "properly". (4): a person of full capacity who advised in writing that they consent, or will not apply, "shall
-- not bring an action against the administrator by reason of his having thereafter distributed" (the baseline's rule).
-- (5): a notice of intention that lapses lets the administrator "act as if he had not received the notice". So a lapsed
-- notice counts as no notice of an intended application (INFERENCE that "act as if" reaches s 20(1)); a notice that an
-- application has been made does not lapse under s 20(5).
GIVEN `the distribution was properly made` IS A BOOLEAN
      `I had notice that an application had been made` IS A BOOLEAN
      `I had notice of an intended application, not lapsed` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the claimant's relationship is not through a legal marriage or adoption` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the claimant advised me in writing that they consent or will not apply` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the claimant was of full legal capacity when they did` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 20(1), (3), (4) -- no action lies against the administrator for the distribution` IF
        (    (NOT `I had notice that an application had been made`)
         AND (NOT `I had notice of an intended application, not lapsed`)
         AND (`the distribution was properly made` OR `the claimant's relationship is not through a legal marriage or adoption`))
    OR  `Have I lost my action against the administrator` `the claimant advised me in writing that they consent or will not apply` `the claimant was of full legal capacity when they did`

§§ `For every role`

@export What is the last day a claim can be made without the Court's leave (Family Provision Act 1972 (WA) s 7(2)(a))?
GIVEN `my role` IS A Role @desc Which of these describes you
      `probate or administration has been granted in Western Australia` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether probate of the will or letters of administration have been granted in Western Australia, or the Public Trustee has filed an election to administer the estate
      `the date the administrator became entitled to administer the estate in WA` IS A DATE @desc The date of the grant of probate or administration in Western Australia (or the Public Trustee's election)
GIVETH A `Date answer`
`What is the last day to claim without leave` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my role`
    WHEN `I am a family member who may have been left out of the estate, or left too little` THEN
        IF NOT `probate or administration has been granted in Western Australia` THEN `does not arise for you`
        ELSE `by` (`What is the last day I can apply without leave` `the date the administrator became entitled to administer the estate in WA`)
    WHEN `I take a share of the estate under the will or on intestacy` THEN
        IF NOT `probate or administration has been granted in Western Australia` THEN `does not arise for you`
        ELSE `by` (`What is the last day I can apply without leave` `the date the administrator became entitled to administer the estate in WA`)
    WHEN `I am the executor or administrator of the estate` THEN
        IF NOT `probate or administration has been granted in Western Australia` THEN `does not arise for you`
        ELSE `by` (`What is the last day I can apply without leave` `the date the administrator became entitled to administer the estate in WA`)

§§ `For the family member who may claim`

§§§ `ss 4, 7(1), (2A), 6(1), (2) -- may I claim, and can the will shut me out`

@export May I claim provision out of the estate (Family Provision Act 1972 (WA) s 7(1), (2A))?
GIVEN `my role` IS A Role @desc Which of these describes you
      `my relationship to the deceased` IS A Relationship @desc How you were related to the person who died: their spouse or de facto partner at the death; a former spouse or de facto partner; their child; their grandchild; a child of their spouse or partner who is not their child; their parent; or another relative, a friend or a charity
      `when I was born` IS A `When I was born` @desc For a child or grandchild, when you were born: before the death, within 10 months after it, or later
      `the deceased was maintaining me wholly or partly just before the death` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the deceased was maintaining you, wholly or partly, immediately before the death
      `I was entitled to be maintained by the deceased at the death` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you were entitled to maintenance from the deceased at the death, by a court order, an agreement or otherwise
      `my parent, a child of the deceased, died before the deceased` IS A BOOLEAN @desc For a grandchild, whether your parent who was the deceased's child died before the deceased
      `I was alive when the deceased married or began living with my parent` IS A BOOLEAN @desc For a child of the deceased's spouse or partner, whether you were alive when the deceased married, or began a de facto relationship with, your parent
      `the deceased took property from my parent's estate, not as a creditor` IS A BOOLEAN @desc For a stepchild, whether the deceased received, or was entitled to receive, property from your parent's estate other than as a creditor
      `the value of that property at my parent's death` IS A NUMBER @desc For a stepchild, the value of that property at your parent's death, in dollars
      `the parentage I rely on was admitted or established in the parent's lifetime` IS A BOOLEAN @desc For a child, grandchild or stepchild, whether the parentage you rely on was admitted by, or established against, the parent in the parent's lifetime
      `the parentage I rely on arises under the Artificial Conception Act 1985` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether that parentage arises under the Artificial Conception Act 1985
      `as the parent, my parentage was admitted by the deceased as an adult or established in their lifetime` IS A BOOLEAN @desc For a parent of the deceased, whether the deceased admitted the relationship as an adult, or it was established in the deceased's lifetime
      `the date of death` IS A DATE @desc The date the person died
      `the prescribed amount` IS A NUMBER @desc The amount prescribed by regulation for s 7(1)(eb), in dollars (not deposited)
GIVETH A `Standing answer`
`May I make a family provision claim` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my role`
    WHEN `I am a family member who may have been left out of the estate, or left too little` THEN `my standing is` (`May I claim against the estate` (`the position built from` `my relationship to the deceased` `when I was born` `the deceased was maintaining me wholly or partly just before the death` `I was entitled to be maintained by the deceased at the death` `my parent, a child of the deceased, died before the deceased` `I was alive when the deceased married or began living with my parent` `the deceased took property from my parent's estate, not as a creditor` `the value of that property at my parent's death` `the parentage I rely on was admitted or established in the parent's lifetime` `the parentage I rely on arises under the Artificial Conception Act 1985` `as the parent, my parentage was admitted by the deceased as an adult or established in their lifetime`) `the date of death` `the prescribed amount`)
    OTHERWISE `does not arise for you`

-- The baseline answers no whatever the two facts are; they are still asked, as there.
@export Can the will, or the estate passing under the intestacy rules, shut out my claim (Family Provision Act 1972 (WA) s 6(1), (2))?
GIVEN `my role` IS A Role @desc Which of these describes you
      `the will says I am to have nothing and make no claim` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the will excludes you or forbids a claim
      `the estate passed wholly or partly on intestacy` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether some or all of the estate passed under the intestacy rules
GIVETH A `Yes or no`
`Can the will or the intestacy shut me out` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my role`
    WHEN `I am a family member who may have been left out of the estate, or left too little` THEN `yes if` (`Can the will or the intestacy shut out my claim` `the will says I am to have nothing and make no claim` `the estate passed wholly or partly on intestacy`)
    OTHERWISE `does not arise for you`

§§§ `ss 7(2), (3), 6(1), (3), (4), 7A, 6(5) -- my application`

@export Will my application be heard, or is it out of time (Family Provision Act 1972 (WA) s 7(2), (3))?
GIVEN `my role` IS A Role @desc Which of these describes you
      `probate or administration has been granted in Western Australia` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether probate of the will or letters of administration have been granted in Western Australia, or the Public Trustee has filed an election to administer the estate
      `the date the administrator became entitled to administer the estate in WA` IS A DATE @desc The date of the grant of probate or administration in Western Australia (or the Public Trustee's election)
      `the date I file my application` IS A DATE @desc The date you file, or will file, your application in the Supreme Court
      `the Court has given me leave to file out of time` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the Court, satisfied the justice of the case requires it, has given you leave to file out of time
GIVETH A `Timing answer`
`Will my claim be heard, or is it out of time` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my role`
    WHEN `I am a family member who may have been left out of the estate, or left too little` THEN
        IF NOT `probate or administration has been granted in Western Australia` THEN `does not arise for you`
        ELSE `my application is` (`Is my application in time` `the date the administrator became entitled to administer the estate in WA` `the date I file my application` `the Court has given me leave to file out of time`)
    OTHERWISE `does not arise for you`

-- The baseline takes the claimant's standing and timing as its own answer types, so they are asked here as the answers
-- to the two questions above (the form can carry them over); the rest are the Court's judgments, asked as facts.
@export Can the Supreme Court order provision for me out of the estate (Family Provision Act 1972 (WA) s 6(1), (3), (4))?
GIVEN `my role` IS A Role @desc Which of these describes you
      `my standing` IS A Standing @desc The answer to "May I claim provision out of the estate?"
      `an application has been made by me or on my behalf` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you (or someone for you) have applied to the Supreme Court
      `my timing` IS A Timing @desc The answer to "Will my application be heard, or is it out of time?"
      `the Court is of the opinion that adequate provision was not made for me` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the Court is of the opinion that the will or intestacy does not make adequate provision for your proper maintenance, support, education or advancement in life
      `the Court refuses on my character or conduct or another sufficient ground` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the Court refuses an order on the ground of your character or conduct, or another ground it thinks sufficient
GIVETH AN `Outcome answer`
`Can the Court order provision out of the estate for me` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my role`
    WHEN `I am a family member who may have been left out of the estate, or left too little` THEN `the Court's power` (`Can the Court order provision for me` `my standing` `an application has been made by me or on my behalf` `my timing` `the Court is of the opinion that adequate provision was not made for me` `the Court refuses on my character or conduct or another sufficient ground`)
    OTHERWISE `does not arise for you`

-- The situation is the baseline's "an application under section 6(1) is before the Court", so within it that input is
-- TRUE.
@export May the Court make an interim order for my immediate needs before it decides my claim (Family Provision Act 1972 (WA) s 7A)?
GIVEN `my role` IS A Role @desc Which of these describes you
      `I have applied to the Court and my claim is undecided` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you have made a claim for provision to the Supreme Court and it has not yet been decided
      `I was totally or partially dependent on the deceased immediately before the death` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you depended on the deceased, wholly or in part, just before the death
      `the Court is of the opinion an interim order is necessary for my immediate needs` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the Court thinks an interim order is necessary for things immediately needed for your maintenance, support or education
GIVETH A `Yes or no`
`May the Court give me an interim order` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my role`
    WHEN `I am a family member who may have been left out of the estate, or left too little` THEN
        IF NOT `I have applied to the Court and my claim is undecided` THEN `does not arise for you`
        ELSE `yes if` (`May the Court make an interim order for me` TRUE `I was totally or partially dependent on the deceased immediately before the death` `the Court is of the opinion an interim order is necessary for my immediate needs`)
    OTHERWISE `does not arise for you`

-- The situation is the baseline's "the evidence did not reveal the property", so within it that input is TRUE.
@export May I bring a further claim because property of the estate was not disclosed (Family Provision Act 1972 (WA) s 6(5), (7))?
GIVEN `my role` IS A Role @desc Which of these describes you
      `estate property the evidence on my claim did not reveal has come to light` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether property of the estate has come to light that the evidence about the estate's nature and extent did not reveal
      `an order was or could have been made for me` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether an order was made, or could have been made, for you on your first claim
      `the Court finds its value would have materially affected my provision` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the Court finds the property's value would have materially affected your provision
      `the date I became aware of the property` IS A DATE @desc When you became aware the property existed
      `the date I file the further claim` IS A DATE @desc When you file, or will file, the further application
      `the Court gives leave to file the further claim out of time` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the Court gives leave because the justice of the case requires it
GIVETH A `Yes or no`
`May I make a further claim for undisclosed property` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my role`
    WHEN `I am a family member who may have been left out of the estate, or left too little` THEN
        IF NOT `estate property the evidence on my claim did not reveal has come to light` THEN `does not arise for you`
        ELSE `yes if` (`May I bring a further claim for undisclosed property` `an order was or could have been made for me` TRUE `the Court finds its value would have materially affected my provision` `the date I became aware of the property` `the date I file the further claim` `the Court gives leave to file the further claim out of time`)
    OTHERWISE `does not arise for you`

§§§ `ss 14(2), 19 -- once provision is ordered for me (situations: provision ordered; a dealing with it)`

@export How much of the provision ordered for me falls on one beneficiary's share, unless the Court orders otherwise (Family Provision Act 1972 (WA) s 14(2))?
GIVEN `my role` IS A Role @desc Which of these describes you
      `the Court has ordered provision for me` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the Supreme Court has ordered provision for you out of the estate
      `the provision ordered for me` IS A NUMBER @desc The provision ordered for you, in dollars
      `the value of that beneficiary's interest` IS A NUMBER @desc The value of that beneficiary's interest in the estate, in dollars
      `the value of all beneficial interests in the estate` IS A NUMBER @desc The total value of all beneficiaries' interests, in dollars
GIVETH AN `Amount`
`How much of my provision falls on one beneficiary's share` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my role`
    WHEN `I am a family member who may have been left out of the estate, or left too little` THEN
        IF NOT `the Court has ordered provision for me` THEN `does not arise for you`
        ELSE amount (`How much of my provision falls on that share` `the provision ordered for me` `the value of that beneficiary's interest` `the value of all beneficial interests in the estate`)
    OTHERWISE `does not arise for you`

-- The situation asks whether a dealing was given; the baseline's input, whether it was given before the order, is then
-- the one fact left.
@export Is a mortgage, charge or assignment I give over my provision of no effect (Family Provision Act 1972 (WA) s 19)?
GIVEN `my role` IS A Role @desc Which of these describes you
      `I have given a mortgage, charge or assignment over my provision` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you have given, or mean to give, a mortgage, charge or assignment of any kind over provision you claim or have been granted
      `I gave it before the Court made the order` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you gave it before the Court made the order granting the provision
GIVETH A `Yes or no`
`Is my mortgage or assignment of my provision of no effect` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my role`
    WHEN `I am a family member who may have been left out of the estate, or left too little` THEN
        IF NOT `I have given a mortgage, charge or assignment over my provision` THEN `does not arise for you`
        ELSE `yes if` (`Is my dealing with my provision of no effect` `I gave it before the Court made the order`)
    OTHERWISE `does not arise for you`

§§§ `s 20(4), (5) -- my notice to the administrator, and my consent (situations: a notice; a consent)`

@export On what date does a notice of an intended claim lapse, unless the administrator is told by then that the claim has been made (Family Provision Act 1972 (WA) s 20(5))?
GIVEN `my role` IS A Role @desc Which of these describes you
      `the administrator has been given notice of an intended claim` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the executor or administrator (you, or the estate's) has received notice that someone intends to apply under the Act
      `the date the administrator first received the notice` IS A DATE @desc When the administrator first received notice of the intended application
      `the date the administrator became entitled to administer the estate in WA` IS A DATE @desc The date of the grant of probate or administration in Western Australia (or the Public Trustee's election)
GIVETH A `Date answer`
`When does a notice of intended claim lapse` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my role`
    WHEN `I am a family member who may have been left out of the estate, or left too little` THEN
        IF NOT `the administrator has been given notice of an intended claim` THEN `does not arise for you`
        ELSE `on` (`When does my notice of intention lapse` `the date the administrator first received the notice` `the date the administrator became entitled to administer the estate in WA`)
    WHEN `I am the executor or administrator of the estate` THEN
        IF NOT `the administrator has been given notice of an intended claim` THEN `does not arise for you`
        ELSE `on` (`When does my notice of intention lapse` `the date the administrator first received the notice` `the date the administrator became entitled to administer the estate in WA`)
    OTHERWISE `does not arise for you`

-- The situation is the baseline's first input, so within it that input is TRUE.
@export Have I lost the right to sue the administrator for a later distribution, by consenting in writing (Family Provision Act 1972 (WA) s 20(4))?
GIVEN `my role` IS A Role @desc Which of these describes you
      `I advised the administrator in writing that I consent, or that I will not apply` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you told the administrator in writing that you consent to the proposed distribution or will not claim
      `I was of full legal capacity when I did` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you were of full legal capacity at the time
GIVETH A `Yes or no`
`Have I given up my action against the administrator` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my role`
    WHEN `I am a family member who may have been left out of the estate, or left too little` THEN
        IF NOT `I advised the administrator in writing that I consent, or that I will not apply` THEN `does not arise for you`
        ELSE `yes if` (`Have I lost my action against the administrator` TRUE `I was of full legal capacity when I did`)
    OTHERWISE `does not arise for you`

§§ `For a beneficiary of the estate (ss 6, 14(2))`

-- The same rule as the claimant's s 6(1), (2) question, from the other side: no gift in a will is safe from a claim.
@export Can the will protect my gift from a family provision claim (Family Provision Act 1972 (WA) s 6(1), (2))?
GIVEN `my role` IS A Role @desc Which of these describes you
GIVETH A `Yes or no`
`Can the will protect my gift from a claim` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my role`
    WHEN `I take a share of the estate under the will or on intestacy` THEN `yes if` (`Can the will or the intestacy shut out my claim` TRUE FALSE)
    OTHERWISE `does not arise for you`

@export How much of the provision ordered for a claimant falls on my share, unless the Court orders otherwise (Family Provision Act 1972 (WA) s 14(2))?
GIVEN `my role` IS A Role @desc Which of these describes you
      `the Court has ordered provision for a claimant` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the Supreme Court has ordered provision for a claimant out of the estate
      `the provision ordered for the claimant` IS A NUMBER @desc The provision ordered for the claimant, in dollars
      `the value of my interest in the estate` IS A NUMBER @desc The value of your interest in the estate, in dollars
      `the value of all beneficial interests in the estate` IS A NUMBER @desc The total value of all beneficiaries' interests, in dollars
GIVETH AN `Amount`
`How much of the claimant's provision falls on my share` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my role`
    WHEN `I take a share of the estate under the will or on intestacy` THEN
        IF NOT `the Court has ordered provision for a claimant` THEN `does not arise for you`
        ELSE amount (`How much of my provision falls on that share` `the provision ordered for the claimant` `the value of my interest in the estate` `the value of all beneficial interests in the estate`)
    OTHERWISE `does not arise for you`

§§ `For the executor or administrator (s 20)`

@export Can a claimant sue me for distributing the estate (Family Provision Act 1972 (WA) s 20(1), (3), (4), (5))?
GIVEN `my role` IS A Role @desc Which of these describes you
      `I have distributed, or propose to distribute, part of the estate` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you have distributed, or propose to distribute, any part of the estate
      `the distribution was properly made` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the distribution was, or will be, properly made in the administration of the estate
      `I had notice that an application had been made` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether, when you distributed, you had notice that an application under the Act had been made to the Court
      `I had notice of an intended application that had not lapsed` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether, when you distributed, you had notice of an intended application that had not lapsed under s 20(5)
      `the claimant's relationship is not through a legal marriage or adoption` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the claimant's relationship to the deceased is not one determined through a legal marriage or adoption (for example a de facto partner, or a child born outside marriage)
      `the claimant advised me in writing that they consent or will not apply` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the claimant told you in writing that they consent to the distribution, or will not make an application affecting it
      `the claimant was of full legal capacity when they did` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the claimant was of full legal capacity when they told you
GIVETH A `Protection answer`
`Can a claimant sue me for distributing the estate` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my role`
    WHEN `I am the executor or administrator of the estate` THEN
        IF NOT `I have distributed, or propose to distribute, part of the estate` THEN `does not arise for you`
        ELSE IF `s 20(1), (3), (4) -- no action lies against the administrator for the distribution` `the distribution was properly made` `I had notice that an application had been made` `I had notice of an intended application that had not lapsed` `the claimant's relationship is not through a legal marriage or adoption` `the claimant advised me in writing that they consent or will not apply` `the claimant was of full legal capacity when they did`
             THEN `no: section 20 bars that action against you`
             ELSE `section 20 does not bar it: whether the action lies is for the general law`
    OTHERWISE `does not arise for you`

-- s 20(2): "no executor or administrator or trustee shall be under any obligation to inquire as to the existence of any
-- person who could claim an interest in the estate ... by virtue only of the provisions of this Act." Fixed for the role.
@export Must I search for people who might claim under this Act before I distribute (Family Provision Act 1972 (WA) s 20(2))?
GIVEN `my role` IS A Role @desc Which of these describes you
GIVETH A `Yes or no`
`Must I search for possible claimants` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my role`
    WHEN `I am the executor or administrator of the estate` THEN no
    OTHERWISE `does not arise for you`
